# Template for projects/ynab-mcp/secrets.enc.env, which is committed *encrypted*.
# Create it with:  make secrets FILE=projects/ynab-mcp/secrets.enc.env
# Deploying it is just `git push` — the workflow decrypts it to /srv/ynab-mcp/.env
# at 0600 before starting the container, which reads it via env_file.
# Requires `make secrets-ci-init` once, to give CI a key scoped to projects/**.

# A YNAB OAuth application (https://app.ynab.com/settings/developer). Its one
# redirect URI must be exactly https://ynab.waqasali.dev/oauth/ynab/callback.
# Deliberately not a Personal Access Token: a PAT is long-lived, all-budgets and
# full-write, whereas these only let the server run a consent flow you approve.
YNAB_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=
YNAB_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Encrypts the stored YNAB refresh tokens at rest, in ./data/ynab-mcp.db.
# Generate with: openssl rand -base64 32
#
# The nightly backup only walks /srv/*/data, so this key is never in a backup —
# which is what keeps a stolen backup useless, and also means losing it makes a
# restored database unreadable. Changing it orphans every stored token and
# forces the connector to be re-authorized.
ENCRYPTION_KEY=
